      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Diagnostic difficulties are common in sigmoid volvulus. This diagnostic delay contributes to high morbidity and mortality."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "AIM",
          "content": "This paper recognises visible or palpable emptiness of the left iliac fossa as a new clinical sign of sigmoid volvulus. Predictive accuracy of the sign was assessed in this study."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "519 patients with acute abdomen of non-traumatic origin were prospectively studied."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The new sign was present in 24 out of 86 patients (28%) with sigmoid volvulus. It was absent in all those who did not have sigmoid volvulus. The positive predictive value of the sign was 100%."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Emptiness of the left iliac fossa is a valuable diagnostic adjunct. Positive sign is pathognomonic of sigmoid volvulus. Nevertheless, a negative sign warrants further investigations."
        }
      ]},
